<% page_title "Care guide" %>
<% meta description: "How to wear and keep DeNshe jewellery: perfume, water, storage, and what to do if a piece needs a repair." %>

<header class="page-intro">
  <div class="page page--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Keep it</p>
    <h1>A short care guide.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Fashion jewellery is meant to be worn. A few habits keep the finish closer to the day it arrived.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="page">
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Last on, first off</h3>
        <p>Perfume, hairspray, and lotion go on first. Let them dry. Then the jewellery. At night, it comes off before cleanser.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Water is the enemy of shine</h3>
        <p>Take pieces off for the shower, the sea, and the gym. Moisture sits in clasps and behind stones, even on anti-tarnish finishes.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Give each piece its own corner</h3>
        <p>Chains tangle, and stones scratch gold-tone metal. A pouch, a box, or even a clean handkerchief is enough. The jewellery box on this site is for remembering. The real one is a drawer.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Wipe, don’t soak</h3>
        <p>A soft dry cloth after wearing is the whole routine. Skip toothpaste, silver dip, and ultrasonic cleaners unless we have told you a piece can take them.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--sand">
  <div class="page split">
    <div class="split__body">
      <p class="eyebrow">Anti-tarnish</p>
      <h2>A finish, not a spell.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Anti-tarnish pieces resist the usual dulling from air and skin. They still prefer to stay dry, and they still like a cloth at the end of the day. If a finish ever looks tired, write to us before you try to polish it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="split__body">
      <p class="eyebrow">If something gives</p>
      <h2>Tell us early.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A loose stone, a clasp that feels soft, a kada with a nick. <%= link_to "Write to us", contact_path %> with a photograph and the piece name. We would rather see it while it is a small repair.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
